  "body": "Fork synced at v0.18.0 (cut from upstream/main 37482923).\n\n## What changed\n\nA 3D Finish option, **Fill openings** (`fill_openings`, mm, off by default), for the land case in #1196: the finish flies over bolt holes and small pockets at their rim instead of diving down their walls.\n\n**The fill rule** (`crates/motion/src/finishing3d/fill.rs`, new):\n- Sample the model's top-down height field on a grid (cell = width/12, coarsened to at most 4M cells; a width too fine for the model at that cap is refused by name). Cells over no facet read as the model's lowest Z.\n- Grey-scale morphological closing with a flat disk of the stated diameter (Serra 1982; Soille 2003). A cell raised by more than the finish tolerance is an opening cell.\n- A connected group is filled only when it is **closed**: none of it on the grid border, and every bordering cell is material standing at the lid's level (within one cell's 45-degree rise + tol). Slots or valleys that run out to an edge, or a lid that would spill over a lower rim, are never filled.\n- Lids (horizontal rectangles at the closed height, never below the surface) cover the group plus its neighbour ring.\n\n**Safety:** the drive facets are the model's facets, unchanged and first, plus lids, so a path planned on them can rise but never bite the model deeper. Only the path is planned on the lids. The verifier still gets `material.facets` (the real model), so a gouge under a lid is still caught. The path gets a `land: N closed opening(s) narrower than W mm filled at their rim and flown over, not cut ...` note.\n\n**Plumbing:** `OpParams::Finish3D.fill_openings: Option<f64>` (undoable through `EditOperationParams`; sanity refuses a non-finite or non-positive width at the door). The optional `fill_openings` file key is absent when None. The MCP params door carries it (`edit_operation {\"fill_openings\": 5.0}`). The stamp digest gets bytes only when a width is set. There's a \"Fill openings\" field on the 3D Finish page. Geodesic + fill is refused by name, because the lids would be new open boundary for its march. There's no project-file version bump: an older reader ignores the key and cuts the model itself, which is a valid finish, not an unsafe one. The reasoning is in `docs/decisions/1196-finish3d-land-fill.md`.\n\n**Option off is byte-identical:** no file key, no digest bytes, and the generators get `&material.facets` as before. No goldens moved.\n\n## Tests\n- `crates/motion/tests/finish3d_land.rs` (new):\n  - `land_finish_flies_over_the_bolt_holes_and_verifies_on_the_real_plate`: a 40x20x8 plate with two 3.4 mm through holes and a 3 mm ball. Waterline and Parallel with fill on: no tip inside a hole below the top. The deepest ball bite measured on the REAL plate is within tol. The same path sunk 0.5 mm is caught on the real plate. The raster crosses the mouths at the top with fill on and doesn't with it off.\n  - `a_blind_pocket_is_lidded_and_a_gouge_into_its_floor_is_convicted`: off dives to the pocket floor and on never does. A plunge planted through the lid into the pocket floor is caught on the real model.\n  - `an_opening_wider_than_the_width_or_open_to_the_edge_is_not_filled`: a 3 mm width doesn't fill a 3.4 mm hole (output is exactly the model), and an edge-to-edge slot stays open.\n  - `nonsense_widths_are_refused_by_name`: 0, negative, NaN, inf, a too-fine width and an empty model.\n- `crates/app/tests/operations.rs` `finish3d_fill_openings_lands_over_a_pocket_and_verifies_on_the_model`: end to end through `GenerateOperation`. Off rides the pocket floor. On never descends, status Ok (the real-model verify is clean), and the land note is present. A negative width is refused at `CreateOperation`.\n- `crates/app/tests/mcp.rs` `fill_openings_rides_the_params_door_and_undoes`: off by default, set over MCP, 0 refused, generate ok, and undo restores off.\n- Quick gate (`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`) on the final head: green on 0754f88c (motion 190 s, app 599 s, ui 74 s; 0 failed). Clippy `-D warnings` is clean on motion, app and ui.\n\n## Not exercised\n- The reporter's STEP part (not attached). The fixtures are square-hole plates.\n- The finish3d heavy (`--ignored`) envelope lane: no existing generator changed, and the fill is opt-in.\n- The UI field is only compile-checked. No snapshot PNGs changed.\n\nChangelog: 3D Finish can fill closed holes and pockets narrower than a stated width on the planned surface (\"Fill openings\"), flying over them as a land finish while the verifier still judges the real model (#1196)\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFixes #1196\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
